# The reference's relative tab chords (Puffin 0.8.4): Cmd [ and Cmd ] step
# along the strip and STOP at either end; Cmd Opt Left/Right and Ctrl Tab /
# Ctrl Shift Tab cycle and WRAP. All six resolve against the strip's rendered
# order, the same order Cmd 1..9 counts in, so a pinned tab is stepped over
# like any other.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t1","t2","t3","t4"],"active_tab":"t1","pinned_tabs":["t2"],"theme":"dark"}

require_thread t1
wait_frames 20

# Show Previous at the first tab goes nowhere: a step is not a cycle.
key CMD+LEFT_BRACKET
wait_frames 24
require_thread t1

# Show Next walks right, through the pinned t2, and stops at the last tab.
key CMD+RIGHT_BRACKET
wait_frames 24
require_thread t2
key CMD+RIGHT_BRACKET
wait_frames 24
require_thread t3
key CMD+RIGHT_BRACKET
wait_frames 24
require_thread t4
key CMD+RIGHT_BRACKET
wait_frames 24
require_thread t4

# Cycle Forward from the last tab comes round to the first...
key CMD+ALT+RIGHT
wait_frames 24
require_thread t1
# ...and Cycle Backward from the first goes round to the last.
key CMD+ALT+LEFT
wait_frames 24
require_thread t4
key CMD+ALT+LEFT
wait_frames 24
require_thread t3

# Ctrl Tab is the same wrapping cycle on the browser chord.
key CMD+RIGHT_BRACKET
wait_frames 24
require_thread t4
key CTRL+TAB
wait_frames 24
require_thread t1
key CTRL+SHIFT+TAB
wait_frames 24
require_thread t4

# A select, never an open: four tabs went in and four are still here, so the
# last slot is still t4 and the first is still t1.
key CMD+1
wait_frames 24
require_thread t1
key CMD+9
wait_frames 24
require_thread t4
